# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
# Digital Detox (sheet tab "det"). (title, text, quote, source)

DET_EN = [
 ("Start where you are", "Spend today simply observing your digital habits without judgment. What do you reach for? When and why?", "Principle #1: Clutter is costly.", "Cal Newport, Digital Minimalism"),
 ("Define your why", "Get clear on your reasons for doing this detox. Before opening any app today, ask: ‘What am I seeking?’ and ‘When will I know I'm done?’", "This is your life—what do you want to pay attention to?", "Catherine Price, How to Break Up with Your Phone"),
 ("Audit your digital life", "List your most-used apps, sites and platforms. For each, ask: does this nourish me or drain me?", "When you pay attention to something you don’t especially value, it’s not an exaggeration to say that you’re paying with your life.", "Oliver Burkeman, Four Thousand Weeks"),
 ("The notification purge", "Silence non-essential notifications, especially social media, shopping and news.", "The art of being wise is the art of knowing what to overlook.", "W. James in Oliver Burkeman, Meditations for Mortals"),
 ("Curate your feed", "Unfollow accounts that trigger comparison or anxiety. Follow only what uplifts or teaches you.", "Your smartphone is mostly just other people’s agenda for you.", "Emma Seppälä, Sovereign"),
 ("Set screen-free zones", "Designate at least one space in your home (like the dining table or bedroom) as tech-free. Move your charging spot outside your bedroom to discourage late-night scrolling and morning phone checks.", "Fill the center of your life... with things that reward creativity, relationship, and engagement.", "Andy Crouch, The Tech-Wise Family"),
 ("Gratitude pause", "Before checking social media, write down 3 things you're grateful for in your real life.", "Reconnect with a part of you that knows that life doesn’t happen on a screen.", "Catherine Price, How to Break Up with Your Phone"),
 ("Design a mindful morning", "Craft a screen-free morning ritual: meditation, stretching, journaling, or just slow tea.", "When we know what to say no to, we can say yes to the things that matter.", "Ryan Holiday, Stillness Is the Key"),
 ("Single-task your screens", "Use one device for one task at a time. Close the other tabs and let your attention rest in one place.", "Our goal isn’t abstinence; it’s consciousness.", "Catherine Price, How to Break Up with Your Phone"),
 ("Batch your digital tasks", "Check email, social media and messages only at set times, for example twice a day.", "In a world of distraction, focusing is a superpower.", "Ryan Holiday, Discipline Is Destiny"),
 ("Unplugged mealtimes", "Commit to at least one meal a day completely free of digital devices.", "Checking your phone is like picking your nose: there’s nothing wrong with it, but no one should have to watch you do it.", "Catherine Price, How to Break Up with Your Phone"),
 ("Leave your phone behind", "Go somewhere today without your phone: a walk, a café, an errand. Notice how you feel.", "Simply put, humans are not wired to be constantly wired.", "Cal Newport, Digital Minimalism"),
 ("Evening digital sunset", "Turn off all screens 1 to 2 hours before bed. Use this time to stretch, read, or prepare for the next day.", "We wake up before our devices do, and they ‘go to bed’ before we do.", "Andy Crouch, The Tech-Wise Family"),
 ("Tech Shabbat", "Try a half-day digital sabbath. No screens unless essential: immerse yourself in real life.", "A day without the sensory food of e-mail, videos, books, and conversations is a chance to clear our mind.", "Thich Nhat Hanh, Silence"),
 ("Get creative", "Find creative replacements: swap Instagram for sketching, news apps for journaling, TikTok for tea and a book.", "There is nourishment in pursuits that have no purpose—that is their purpose.", "Ryan Holiday, Stillness Is the Key"),
 ("Replace, don't just remove", "Try analog tools for tasks you usually do on a screen. Rediscover the joy of a paper notebook.", "The heart of our home is built around things older and better than the newest thing.", "Andy Crouch, The Tech-Wise Family"),
 ("Reconnect in real life", "Make a call instead of texting. Meet someone in person. Let human connection replace screen time today.", "The socializing that counts is real conversation, and text is no longer a sufficient alternative.", "Cal Newport, Digital Minimalism"),
 ("Relearn boredom", "Notice when you reach for your phone out of boredom. Sit with the urge for a few minutes and see if it passes.", "In Zen they say: If something is boring after two minutes, try it for four... Eventually one discovers that it is not boring at all.", "J. Cage in Jenny Odell, How to Do Nothing"),
 ("Weekend detox challenge", "Try a device-free stretch from Friday evening to Saturday noon. Let this time hold space for real life.", "The world is like muddy water. To see through it, we have to let things settle.", "Ryan Holiday, Stillness Is the Key"),
 ("Craft your digital code", "Write your personal tech manifesto: based on the last 3 weeks, what boundaries and habits will support your values from now on?", "Build a life that you don’t need to escape from.", "Ryan Holiday, Stillness Is the Key"),
 ("Notice what's changed", "Compare today to day 1. Notice what has shifted over these three weeks, and set your own terms for the slip-ups ahead.", "What unplugging lets us do is reflect on the past, present, and future.", "Tiffany Shlain, 24/6"),
]

